SteamARM: textures Metal can compress; render-pass statistics

KosmicKrisp gave every image that can be a transfer destination Metal's
shader-write usage, and that usage keeps a texture out of Metal's lossless
compression. Every transfer write here is a Metal copy or a render pass
(clears, blits, resolves), never a shader, so shader-write is now only for
storage images and atomic formats. Counter-Strike 2 with 4x MSAA, where
every multisampled colour and depth target is stored and loaded again at
each of ~90 render-pass changes a frame (about 2 GB of samples before
compression): the main menu at 44.2 fps before (43.9, 44.0, 44.6), 48.1
after (48.7, 47.0, 48.7), Dust2 48.8 (MEASURED 2026-10-04). Vulkan tests
40/40. KK_IMAGE_COMPRESS=0 restores the old usage.

Not done: the pixel-format-view usage of mutable images stays (Metal
accepts sRGB/UNORM views without it, but KosmicKrisp's own copies and
resolves view images in other formats: without it the game crashed at
start), and so does that of depth/stencil (a stencil view needs it).

KK_PASS_STATS=1 prints every 120 frames the render encoders per frame,
their stores (all and multisampled, in MB before compression) and why
encoders ended (barrier, compute or copy, a pass on other attachments, end
of a pass, state change).
